275563892e-06,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-5.245195097813848e-06,-0.5292089581489563,-1.5243234634399414,-1.728519782773219e-05,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-0.00016902448260225356,-2.7418097943154862e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,23606,400,87,61,18,488,220,23,87,61,17,481,220,19,87,488,272,284,220,15,3,702,2326,19703,11,825,315,892,374,279,2629,315,279,1008,1378,13,3555,374,400,66,3,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe equation $x^3 + 8x^2 - 4x + c = 0$ has three roots, one of which is the sum of the other two. What is $c$?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"5fa7534e02f7c900a7d7aa202cd86fe95cdaf3f22d49c50bc89ae26e00dd4268"},"seconds":42.54793381690979,"seed":428371883840085374,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we will use the relationship between the roots and coefficients of a polynomial. Let the roots of the equation $x^3 + 8x^2 - 4x + c = 0$ be $\\alpha$, $\\beta$, and $\\gamma$.\n\nGiven that one root is the sum of the other two, we can set $\\gamma = \\alpha + \\beta$. \n\nFrom Vieta's formulas, we know:\n1. The sum of the roots $\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = -\\frac{\\text{coefficient of } x^2}{\\text{leading coefficient}} = -8$.\n2. The sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time $\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = \\frac{\\text{coefficient of } x}{\\text{leading coefficient}} = -4$.\n3. The product of the roots $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = -\\frac{\\text{constant term}}{\\text{leading coefficient}} = -c$.\n\nUsing the given $\\gamma = \\alpha + \\beta$, we substitute in the first of Vieta's relations:\n\\[\n\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\alpha + \\beta + (\\alpha + \\beta) = 2(\\alpha + \\beta) = -8.\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n\\alpha + \\beta = -4.\n\\]\n\nNext, using the second Vieta's relation with $\\gamma = \\alpha + \\beta$:\n\\[\n\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = \\alpha\\beta + \\beta(\\alpha + \\beta) + (\\alpha + \\beta)\\alpha = \\alpha\\beta + \\alpha\\beta + \\beta^2 + \\alpha^2 + \\alpha\\beta = 3\\alpha\\beta + \\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = -4.\n\\]\n\nWe know $\\alpha + \\beta = -4$, so $(\\alpha + \\beta)^2 = 16$. Expanding this:\n\\[\n\\alpha^2 + 2\\alpha\\beta + \\beta^2 = 16.\n\\]\n\nSubtracting $2\\alpha\\beta$ from both sides:\n\\[\n\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = 16 - 2\\alpha\\beta.\n\\]\n\nSubstitute $\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2$ back into the equation $3\\alpha\\beta + \\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = -4$:\n\\[\n3\\alpha\\beta + (16 - 2\\alpha\\beta) = -4.\n\\]\nSimplify:\n\\[\n\\alpha\\beta + 16 = -4.\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n\\alpha\\beta = -20.\n\\]\n\nFinally, using the third Vieta's relation:\n\\[\n\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = -c,\n\\]\nwhere $\\gamma = \\alpha + \\beta = -4$:\n\\[\n\\alpha\\beta(-4) = -c \\implies -20 \\cdot -4 = -c \\implies 80 = -c \\implies c = -80.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of $c$ is \\boxed{-80}."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{-80}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To solve the problem, we will use the relationship between the roots and coefficients of a polynomial. Let the roots of the equation $x^3 + 8x^2 - 4x + c = 0$ be $\\alpha$, $\\beta$, and $\\gamma$.\n\nGiven that one root is the sum of the other two, we can set $\\gamma = \\alpha + \\beta$. \n\nFrom Vieta's formulas, we know:\n1. The sum of the roots $\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = -\\frac{\\text{coefficient of } x^2}{\\text{leading coefficient}} = -8$.\n2. The sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time $\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = \\frac{\\text{coefficient of } x}{\\text{leading coefficient}} = -4$.\n3. The product of the roots $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = -\\frac{\\text{constant term}}{\\text{leading coefficient}} = -c$.\n\nUsing the given $\\gamma = \\alpha + \\beta$, we substitute in the first of Vieta's relations:\n\\[\n\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\alpha + \\beta + (\\alpha + \\beta) = 2(\\alpha + \\beta) = -8.\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n\\alpha + \\beta = -4.\n\\]\n\nNext, using the second Vieta's relation with $\\gamma = \\alpha + \\beta$:\n\\[\n\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = \\alpha\\beta + \\beta(\\alpha + \\beta) + (\\alpha + \\beta)\\alpha = \\alpha\\beta + \\alpha\\beta + \\beta^2 + \\alpha^2 + \\alpha\\beta = 3\\alpha\\beta + \\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = -4.\n\\]\n\nWe know $\\alpha + \\beta = -4$, so $(\\alpha + \\beta)^2 = 16$. Expanding this:\n\\[\n\\alpha^2 + 2\\alpha\\beta + \\beta^2 = 16.\n\\]\n\nSubtracting $2\\alpha\\beta$ from both sides:\n\\[\n\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = 16 - 2\\alpha\\beta.\n\\]\n\nSubstitute $\\alpha^2 + \\beta^2$ back into the equation $3\\alpha\\beta + \\alpha^2 + \\beta^2 = -4$:\n\\[\n3\\alpha\\beta + (16 - 2\\alpha\\beta) = -4.\n\\]\nSimplify:\n\\[\n\\alpha\\beta + 16 = -4.\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n\\alpha\\beta = -20.\n\\]\n\nFinally, using the third Vieta's relation:\n\\[\n\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = -c,\n\\]\nwhere $\\gamma = \\alpha + \\beta = -4$:\n\\[\n\\alpha\\beta(-4) = -c \\implies -20 \\cdot -4 = -c \\implies 80 = -c \\implies c = -80.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of $c$ is \\boxed{-80}.","id":"intermediate_algebra:262"}
